{"nodes": [{"id": "title", "type": "text", "text": "Module 18 — Risk Anticipation with Risk Management\nconcepts → program → frameworks → vuln program → scanning → PIA/DPIA", "x": -1200, "y": -3600, "width": 2400, "height": 70, "color": "5"}, {"id": "b1", "type": "text", "text": "LO01 · CONCEPTS  (pp4-11)\n\nRISK MGMT = reduce + MAINTAIN risk at\nACCEPTABLE LEVEL via active program;\nidentify → assess → respond;\nSYSTEM SECURITY LIFE-CYCLE\n\n6 OBJECTIVES: identify · impact ·\nPRIORITIZE by impact/severity · analyse +\nreport · CONTROL + MITIGATE · awareness\n\n7 BENEFITS: impact focus · level-based ·\nprocess · adversity action · resources ·\nREVENUE protection · controls\n\nROLES: senior mgmt supervise · CIO executes\n+ trains · owners monitor + config mgmt ·\nfunctional mgrs TRADE-OFF DECISIONS ·\nISSOs · practitioners · trainers\n\nKRI = metric of ACTIVITY RISKINESS,\nearly-stage health indicator\n  triad: define risk · adverse possibility ·\n  EARLY WARNING\n  4 FEATURES: QUANTIFIABLE · PREDICTABLE\n  · COMPARABLE · INFORMATIONAL\nKPI = progress-toward-goals metric +\nLEADING INDICATOR; KRIs reflect KPI\nimpact, escalate on LEVELS", "x": -2400, "y": -3420, "width": 600, "height": 700}, {"id": "b2", "type": "text", "text": "LO02 · CONTEXT → MATRIX  (pp12-18)\n\nCONTEXT: posture + external/internal env\nIDENTIFICATION = FOUNDATION + FIRST STEP\n  before-harm listing; skill-dependent;\n  sources/causes/consequences; RISK\n  REGISTER; ITERATIVE; threats vs\n  opportunities\n  elements: DESCRIPTION/EVENT · CAUSES ·\n  CONSEQUENCES; checklists, flow charts,\n  systems analysis\nASSESSMENT: likelihood × impact; ONGOING\nITERATIVE; bands 1–2 kill in 24H · 3–4\nreasonable time · 5–6 ASAP\nANALYSIS: inherent vs CONTROLLED; nature;\nsame-severity prioritization\n\nTABLE 18.1 LEVELS (p17)\n  Extreme/High: ISOLATE, ELIMINATE,\n    SUBSTITUTE immediately\n  Med-upper: controls + STRICT TIMELINES,\n    system RUNS\n  Med-lower: STOP THE ACTIVITY\n  Low: quick measures / preventive +\n    PERIODICAL REVIEW\n\nMATRIX (p18)\n  RATING = PROBABILITY × SEVERITY\n  bands 81–100% → 1–20%; classes severe /\nmajor / moderate / minor / insignificant\n  tolerable vs non-tolerable lines", "x": -1740, "y": -3420, "width": 600, "height": 700}, {"id": "b3", "type": "text", "text": "LO02 · TREATMENT → TRACKING  (pp19-24)\n\nTREATMENT = select + implement controls\nto MODIFY out-of-tolerance risks;\npre-list: method, owners, costs, benefits,\nsuccess odds, measurement\n\np19 FOUR WORDINGS\n  avoiding (skip the activity) · reducing\n  (likelihood + impact) · TRANSFERRING\n  (INSURANCE or partnership) · accepting\n  (cannot avoid/transfer)\n\np21 SIX OPTIONS\n  ELIMINATE (threat-to-zero) · TRANSFER\n  (third party) · MITIGATE (direct or\n  competing controls) · ACCEPT (action\n  costs > impact) · AVOIDANCE (eg NO\n  LAPTOPS) · REDUCE (likelihood)\n  stakeholders + owners DECIDE; RESIDUAL\n  RISKS persist\n\n  ✗ the two lists are NEVER MAPPED\n\nPLAN (p23) = responses + owners + TARGET\nDATES; ESSENTIAL ISO 27001 document\nTRACKING (new risks; prob/impact/status)\nvs REVIEW (effectiveness)", "x": -1080, "y": -3420, "width": 600, "height": 700}, {"id": "b4", "type": "text", "text": "LO03 · ERM + NIST + COSO  (pp25-33)\n\nRMF = UNDERSTAND OVERALL RISK LEVEL\nERM (pp27-28): planning, organizing,\nleading, controlling\n  events → likelihood/impact → strategy\n  → monitor\n  9 KEY ACTIVITIES IN ORDER\n    classification → control selection →\n    refinement → SYSTEM SECURITY PLAN →\n    implementation → assessment →\n    agency-risk decision → AUTHORIZATION\n    → CONTINUOUS MONITORING\n  10 GOALS (p29)\n\nNIST RMF (pp30-31): 7 tasks + assessment\nsub-steps + authorize/monitor;\nhttps://csrc.nist.gov (prose form)\n\nCOSO ERM (pp32-33): origin + FOUR prose\ncomponents\n  ✗ fifth lives only in garbled tiles\n\nenterprise network RM (p26): 4 defender\nsteps (identify → procedures → mitigate\n→ policies/checklists)", "x": -420, "y": -3420, "width": 600, "height": 700}, {"id": "b5", "type": "text", "text": "LO03 · GOVERNANCE + VENDORS  (pp34-42)\n\nCOBIT: stakeholders, principles,\nobjectives, cascade, components, focus\nareas (tails truncated, recorded)\nPOLICY (p38) objectives\nBEST PRACTICES (p39) incl. KRIs\nVENDORS, prose Source: lines ONLY\n  SAS · LogicManager · Enablon · Acuity\n  ✗ tile URLs garbled → refused\n  (sas.can, wofterskluwer.corn …)", "x": 240, "y": -3420, "width": 600, "height": 700}, {"id": "b6", "type": "text", "text": "LO04 · VULN PROGRAM  (pp43-50)\n\nRMFs REQUIRE a vuln-mgmt program\n(Tripwire source, p44)\nPHASES (prose): assessment · REPORTING\n(technical + executive) · REMEDIATION\n(treating risks); DISCOVERY FIRST (p47:\nidentify assets/components)\n  ✗ figure order garbled → only\n  Discovery-first asserted\nPRIORITIZATION (p49): importance on\n0–5 SCALE\n  dashboards (OSSIM pp48-50) = NON-EVIDENCE", "x": 900, "y": -3420, "width": 600, "height": 700}, {"id": "b7", "type": "text", "text": "LO04 · ASSESS → VERIFY  (pp51-57)\n\nASSESSMENT (p51) = find BEFORE attackers;\nreport contents · benefits · steps ·\nscheduling (p52)\n\nMITIGATION vs REMEDIATION vs VERIFY\n  MITIGATION acts WITHOUT FIXING:\n    WAF instead of fixing the web app (p53)\n  REMEDIATION CORRECTS the vuln (p54)\n  VERIFICATION PROVES solved (p55)\n  extra solutions: Qualys · Skybox\n  (SCAN-LESS assessment)\n  dashboards = NON-EVIDENCE", "x": -2400, "y": -2620, "width": 620, "height": 700, "color": "4"}, {"id": "b8", "type": "text", "text": "LO05 · SCANNING  (pp58-64)\n\nEXTERNAL (p59): internet-facing exam;\nnmap command kept, garbled output\nrefused\nFOUR STAGES (p60) prints THREE bullets\n(plan/configure · resolve · baseline) —\nfourth label ABSENT\nINTERNAL (p61): password complexity, AV;\nheader refused, names from p62 prose\nSCANNERS: OWASP ZAP · WebInspect\n(printed Weblnspect) · AppScan · Qualys ·\nVega — crawl then report, toward\nVULNERABILITY-FREE sites; dynamic\ncoverage beyond black-box", "x": -1740, "y": -2620, "width": 620, "height": 700}, {"id": "b9", "type": "text", "text": "LO06 · PIA/DPIA  (pp65-71)\n\nDPIA (p66) = STRUCTURED, SYSTEMATIC\nprivacy-risk assessment; 9 STEPS:\nneed → describe → consult →\nnecessity (label truncated 'onality') →\nrisks → measures → sign-off →\nintegrate → KEEP UNDER REVIEW\nPIA (p68) = ID + address data-protection\nrisks, new or existing projects\n  3 OBJECTIVES: legal adherence ·\n  breach-risk ID · alternatives\n  4 TRIGGERS: new PII tech · risky data ·\n  system updates · PII rulemaking\n12 PIA STEPS (pp69-70); PIA inside RM\n(p71); 'hams' kept verbatim", "x": -1080, "y": -2620, "width": 620, "height": 700}, {"id": "b10", "type": "text", "text": "LO06 · TOOLS + SUMMARY  (pp72-78)\n\nprose ONLY: Mandatly (case-scenario ID)\n· Seers (risk mapping) · OneTrust ·\nTrustArc · Privado (real-time flows) ·\nSmartsheet · PrivacyEngine · Collibra\n  URLs quoted DAMAGED (privahai,\nsmartsheet.corn, spaced schemes)\n  dashboards (pp72-74) = NON-EVIDENCE\nPIA vs ASSESSMENT (p77): PIA cuts\npersonal-info risks, MANDATORY with\npersonal info; framework = internal\nEARLY-WARNING system\nSUMMARY (p78): risk mgmt = reduce +\nMAINTAIN at acceptable level, active\nprogram", "x": -420, "y": -2620, "width": 620, "height": 700}, {"id": "pat", "type": "text", "text": "THE MODULE'S FIVE TRAPS\n\n1 · TWO TREATMENT LISTS, NEVER MAPPED\n  p19 (avoid/reduce/transfer/accept) vs p21\n  (Eliminate/Transfer/Mitigate/Accept +\n  Avoidance/Reduce) — which-page test\n2 · MITIGATE ≠ FIX\n  WAF instead of fixing = mitigation;\n  remediation corrects; verification proves\n3 · MISSING LABELS\n  Four Stages prints three; COSO fifth is\n  figure-only garble; Phase-4-style gaps\n  are never filled\n4 · MATRIX INTERIOR\n  reconstructed from linear OCR — bands,\n  classes, formula exact; cells uncertain\n5 · PRINTED DAMAGE, KEPT VERBATIM\n  Weblnspect · hams · privahai ·\n  smartsheet.corn · spaced https · EGit ·\n  sas.can — recorded, never repaired", "x": 240, "y": -2620, "width": 1320, "height": 700, "color": "6"}], "edges": [{"id": "e1", "fromNode": "b1", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "b2", "toSide": "left"}, {"id": "e2", "fromNode": "b2", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "b3", "toSide": "left"}, {"id": "e3", "fromNode": "b3", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "b4", "toSide": "left"}, {"id": "e4", "fromNode": "b4", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "b5", "toSide": "left"}, {"id": "e5", "fromNode": "b5", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "b6", "toSide": "left"}, {"id": "e6", "fromNode": "b6", "fromSide": "bottom", "toNode": "b7", "toSide": "top"}, {"id": "e7", "fromNode": "b7", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "b8", "toSide": "left"}, {"id": "e8", "fromNode": "b8", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "b9", "toSide": "left"}, {"id": "e9", "fromNode": "b9", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "b10", "toSide": "left"}, {"id": "e10", "fromNode": "b10", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "pat", "toSide": "left"}]}